Implement io_service_get_matching_service, whose stub failed every IOSurfaceCreate.

IOServiceGetMatchingService is the SINGULAR lookup, and all three of its wire forms (plain, ool,
bin) were stubs returning KERN_NOT_SUPPORTED while the PLURAL iterator form worked. IOSurface
+initialize is the first caller in this system: the stub meant g_surfaceService stayed 0, every
IOSurfaceCreate failed with MACH_SEND_INVALID_DEST, Qt retained the resulting NULL surface
unchecked, and CMake.app died in CFRetain at its first paint.

The three forms share one helper against the same ServiceRegistry the iterator uses. The
unserializer is chosen by CONTENT rather than by wire form, because the client picks the form by
SIZE and the encoding by its own flags, so either form can carry either encoding.

No match answers success with a null port, mirroring what the client already treats as absence.
A match hands the client one send right; a registered service keeps the right its constructor
made, so no-senders cannot destroy it underneath the registry.

Task #227.
